  "final": {
    "headline": "Klein Cain Defeats Tomball, 55–38, on Homecoming Night",
    "byline": "Cain Game Day desk · Updated 10:35 PM CT",
    "body": "Klein Cain opened district play with its most convincing statement of the season, powering past Tomball, 55–38, on Sept. 18 before a capacity homecoming crowd at Klein Memorial Stadium. The victory lifted the Hurricanes to 3–0 and emphatically reversed Dave Campbell’s Texas Football computer projection that had favored the Cougars by three; Cain instead dictated terms from the opening snap to win by seventeen.\n\nBefore kickoff, quarterbacks coach Aiden Upchurch stressed that disciplined execution, not homecoming emotion, would decide the district opener against a respected Tomball team. “Our key to victory tonight will be our level of execution,” Upchurch said before kickoff. Cain followed that script faithfully. Junior quarterback Jace Hanks directed the offense with poise throughout the night, firing four touchdown passes and balancing an explosive ground game led by Eyan Johnson’s 190 rushing yards.\n\nThe rivalry duel turned physical in the fourth quarter as Cain pulled away. Personal fouls mounted and tempers flared on both sidelines, culminating in the fourth-quarter ejection of senior Earl Oguinn Jr. following a scuffle. Even with the late friction, the Hurricanes closed out an authoritative district-opening win to stay unbeaten atop District 15-6A.",
